# Kyno licensing

This repository contains code under two licenses. The full texts live in
the LICENSES directory, and every source file names its license in an
SPDX-License-Identifier header.

MIT — the integration surface, which you are welcome to copy, fork, and
build on:

- src/kyno/sdk/
- src/kyno/adapters/
- src/kyno/conformance/
- conformance/
- docs/integrating.md

Elastic License 2.0 — the control plane (the server, store, CLI, and
publishing). You can use it, read it, change it, self-host it in
production, and build on it for free. The one thing it does not permit is
offering Kyno itself to third parties as a hosted or managed service.

Anything not listed above is under the Elastic License 2.0.
